REM Protects single-line IF/FI forms the compiler accepts from a false line-break
REM diagnostic: a labelled single-line IF with a semicolon-chained branch and a
REM jump back to its own label, a nested single-line IF closed by two chained FI,
REM IF...THEN RETURN...FI, a nested single-line IF/FI followed on the same line
REM by the outer ELSE, a nested single-line IF/ELSE/FI followed on the same line
REM by the outer ELSE, ELSE-only nesting with no inner end-of-IF, and the same
REM nested one-liner continued over colon-prefixed lines, each in upper, lower
REM and mixed case. Also protects a colon-continued ELSE-IF chain inside a
REM DEF FN body with no explicit FI anywhere, closed only by FNEND.
loopstart: IF flag THEN count = 1; GOTO loopstart
loopstart2: if flag then count = 2; goto loopstart2
LoopStart3: If flag Then count = 3; Goto loopstart3
IF flag THEN IF other THEN count = 4 FI FI
if flag then if other then count = 5 fi fi
If flag Then If other Then count = 6 Fi Fi
IF flag THEN RETURN 1 FI
if flag then return 2 fi
If flag Then Return 3 Fi
IF flag THEN IF other THEN count = 7 FI ELSE count = 8 FI
if flag then if other then count = 9 fi else count = 10 fi
If flag Then If other Then count = 11 Fi Else count = 12 Fi
IF flag THEN IF other THEN count = 13 ELSE count = 14 FI ELSE count = 15 FI
if flag then if other then count = 16 else count = 17 fi else count = 18 fi
If flag Then If other Then count = 19 Else count = 20 Fi Else count = 21 Fi
IF flag THEN IF other THEN count = 22 ELSE count = 23 ELSE count = 24
if flag then if other then count = 25 else count = 26 else count = 27
If flag Then If other Then count = 28 Else count = 29 Else count = 30
IF flag THEN
: IF other THEN count = 31 ELSE count = 32 FI
: ELSE count = 33 FI
if flag then
: if other then count = 34 else count = 35 fi
: else count = 36 fi
If flag Then
: If other Then count = 37 Else count = 38 Fi
: Else count = 39 Fi

def fnwidgetlabel$(qty)
if len(qty)=4 then
: return str(qty:"9999")
: else if len(qty)=3 then
: return str(qty:"999")
: else return qty
fnend
